;; Use case: the vocabulary of types.
;;
;; Every type a document can have (definition, deduction, belief…) is itself defined by a
;; document of type :definition, named `type-<type>`. A badge showing a type points at it.
;; The closed publication `vocabulaire-des-types` holds them, in one version per language.
;; In prod it had no language: the fr version keeps its id; the en version gets a new id and
;; an English title. `type-publication` came later. A closed publication takes no new
;; document, so it is published in its own closed publication,
;; `vocabulaire-des-types-la-publication`, not copied from prod.
;;
;; Data copied from the prod database (AGORA_DOCUMENT), 2026-10-18.
